{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/pulls/7208","id":4838770009,"node_id":"PR_kwDOS4Me3c8AAAABIGnFWQ","html_url":"https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate/pull/7208","diff_url":"https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate/pull/7208.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate/pull/7208.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/issues/7208","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/pulls/7208/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/pulls/7208/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/issues/7208/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/statuses/0648e4a371156b819b2c40e9b078c6cc6535e5f7","number":7208,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(omp): restore watcher continuity across superseded confirmations and dead arm children","user":{"login":"i098","id":70973465,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTczNDY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70973465?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098","html_url":"https://github.com/i098","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #7207\n\n## Intent\n\nPort the merged Pi watcher-continuity fix to the omp watch extension (.omp/extensions/fm-primary-omp-watch.ts). Today a handling confirmation that exits 3 (the recovery marker already moved to another generation, meaning a newer pipeline owns the episode) is reported to the primary as 'watcher: FAILED - handling delivery confirmation was rejected (status=3 ...)' on a wake that delivered fine, so the primary spends turns on a non-failure. It must deliver the wake plain, confirm and retry against the restoration's own recovery token, and retire the current arm only when the failed token names its exact watcher pid and generation and that pid is dead. Also, an arm child whose process is gone but whose close event has not fired (a straggler holds its stdio pipes) keeps the single-flight slot, so repair (fm_watch_arm_omp) and scheduled retry answer 'unchanged' and start nothing; such a child must count as an empty slot, as on Pi (liveArmChild). Restore only: no new knob and no default change; OpenCode keeps its current behavior.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- `.omp/extensions/fm-primary-omp-watch.ts` now ports the Pi contract from #5489 (closing #5492).\n  A handling confirmation that exits 3 means the recovery marker moved to another generation, so a newer pipeline owns the episode.\n  omp delivers that wake plain, with no `watcher: FAILED - handling delivery confirmation was rejected (status=3 ...)` line.\n- omp confirms and retries against the restoration's own recovery token, not a fresh snapshot of the current arm child.\n  After a failed confirmation it retires the current arm only when the failed token names that arm's exact watcher pid and generation and that pid is dead.\n- `liveArmChild` treats an arm child whose process is gone, but whose close event has not fired because a straggler holds its stdio, as an empty slot.\n  Repair, scheduled retry, and deferred close start a fresh arm instead of answering \"unchanged\".\n- `docs/watcher-continuity.md` scopes those sentences to Pi and omp.\n  OpenCode has the same gap and is not touched here.\n- Three tests in `tests/fm-omp-harness.test.sh`, each failing on `main` and passing here:\n  a superseded confirmation (exit 3) is not a failure while a refused one (exit 1) still is;\n  a failed confirmation for a stale successor spares a newer arm;\n  a dead-but-unclosed arm child frees the slot for repair and for the scheduled retry.\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n✅ Low: This restores existing Pi behavior in the omp extension, with no new setting and no default change.\nThe retire guard now acts on fewer cases than before, never more.\nThe deferred-close path uses the same `liveArmChild` call as repair and retry, and it has no test of its own.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun before and after, with a Node host running the real extension over a fake omp API and a stub `bin/fm-watch-arm.sh`:\n\n| Case | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| confirmation exits 3 | wake ends with `watcher: FAILED - handling delivery confirmation was rejected (status=3 generation=gen-1 ...)` | plain wake, no failure text |\n| confirmation exits 1 | `rejected (status=1 ...)` | unchanged |\n| failed confirmation while a newer arm runs | `main` retires the current arm once the failed token's watcher pid is dead, newer or not | the newer healthy arm survives |\n| arm exits while a straggler holds its pipes, then `fm_watch_arm_omp` | `unchanged - omp extension already owns an arm child` | `started omp extension arm child` |\n\nThe retire-guard test also fails when only the pid and generation check is removed.\n\n`bin/fm-test-run.sh --all` on Linux with no ruby and no agent harness installed, detached from omp: 254 scripts, 16 fail.\nThe same 16 fail the same way on clean `main` `20dcbf91`, so this change adds no failure:\n`fm-backend-herdr-presentation-e2e`, `fm-ci-workflow`, `fm-control-relaunch`, `fm-extension-binding`, `fm-harness-liveness-drift-live-e2e`, `fm-nm-test-contract`, `fm-pr-check-security`, `fm-procevent-quota`, `fm-procevent`, `fm-public-followup`, `fm-remote-secondmate-lifecycle-e2e`, `fm-remote-transport-lanes`, `fm-secondmate-restart`, `fm-session-lock-ancestry`, `fm-supervision-host`, `fm-test-run`.\nTwo of them print `ruby is required`, and one prints `no verified harness is installed here`.\n`tests/fm-omp-harness.test.sh` passes when run detached from omp.\nIt fails when run from inside an omp session, on `main` and here alike, because its detection test sees the real omp ancestor.\n\nLive validation: one scenario ran live, a real omp 18.7.0 that loaded the changed extension, armed a watcher through it, started a successor, and delivered one wake.\nThe other four scenarios (exit 3, exit 1, the newer-arm guard, the dead-child slot) ran only in the fixture host, with a fake omp API, real arm child processes, and the real confirm script.\nThe Test step therefore reports the live-validation verdict as inconclusive.\nThe merged Pi PR shipped with the same limitation.\n\n## Pipeline\n\nUpdates from [git push no-mistakes](https://github.com/kunchenguid/no-mistakes)\n\n<!-- no-mistakes-pipeline-attestation:v1 {\"head_sha\":\"0648e4a371156b819b2c40e9b078c6cc6535e5f7\",\"steps\":[{\"step\":\"intent\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"rebase\",\"status\":\"skipped\"},{\"step\":\"review\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"test\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"document\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"lint\",\"status\":\"skipped\"},{\"step\":\"push\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"pr\",\"status\":\"running\"},{\"step\":\"ci\",\"status\":\"pending\"}],\"live_validation\":{\"verdict\":\"inconclusive\",\"live\":0,\"total\":4}} -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **intent** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⏭️ **Rebase** - skipped</summary>\n\nStep was skipped.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Review** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚠️ **Test** - 2 warnings</summary>\n\n- ⚠️ `tests/fm-omp-primary-live-e2e.test.sh` - The live omp e2e (`FM_OMP_LIVE_E2E=1 tests/fm-omp-primary-live-e2e.test.sh`, real omp 18.12.1 over RPC, started from a clean tmux ancestor) fails at its step 2: &#39;the session-start digest did not reach model context before the first turn&#39;. The model replied that no digest was present, and the log shows one `extension_error` frame. This is before the arm/deliver steps, so no live watch scenario could be reached. The diff changes only `.omp/extensions/fm-primary-omp-watch.ts`, `docs/watcher-continuity.md` and `tests/fm-omp-harness.test.sh`, so this looks like omp 18.12.1 drift or an environment issue. I did not run the script on the base commit to confirm that. The portable suite, which runs the same extension over a fake omp API, passes fully from a clean ancestor.\n- ⚠️ live validation verdict: inconclusive (0 of 4 scenarios were driven live against the product); untested: A handling confirmation exiting 3 delivers a plain wake with no &#39;watcher: FAILED&#39; appendix, while an exit-1 refusal still reports the failure, A failed confirmation retries on its own recovery token and retires only an arm whose pid and generation match and whose pid is dead; a newer healthy arm survives, A scheduled retry and repair both treat a dead-but-unclosed arm child as an empty slot, Existing watch-extension behaviours unchanged: supervision host in away and quiet modes, opt-out, replacement replay, split host close\n- Live validation: ⚠️ inconclusive - 0 of 4 scenarios driven live against the product\n\n| Scenario | Result | Live | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A handling confirmation exiting 3 delivers a plain wake with no &#39;watcher: FAILED&#39; appendix, while an exit-1 refusal still reports the failure | ⏸️ untested | no | The live omp e2e fails at its session-start-digest step (step 2) with real omp 18.12.1, before any arm or confirmation step. I tried a clean-ancestor tmux run, which reached the same result. Making th… |\n| A failed confirmation retries on its own recovery token and retires only an arm whose pid and generation match and whose pid is dead; a newer healthy arm survives | ⏸️ untested | no | Same blocker: the live omp e2e fails at its session-start-digest step before reaching any watch step, so a stale-successor lab case on the real omp could not be built on a passing live base. |\n| A scheduled retry and repair both treat a dead-but-unclosed arm child as an empty slot | ⏸️ untested | no | Same blocker: the live e2e does not get past its session-start-digest step, so SIGKILLing the arm child on the real omp could not be driven. |\n| Existing watch-extension behaviours unchanged: supervision host in away and quiet modes, opt-out, replacement replay, split host close | ⏸️ untested | no | Same blocker: the live e2e does not reach the arm-and-deliver step with real omp 18.12.1. |\n\n- <code>`env -u NO_MISTAKES_GATE TMUX_TMPDIR=$LAB/tmux tmux -L fm-lab new-session ... FM_OMP_LIVE_E2E=1 bash tests/fm-omp-primary-live-e2e.test.sh` (real omp 18.12.1): step 1 ok (both extensions auto-discovered), step 2 not ok (session-start digest), exit 1</code>\n- <code>`bash tests/fm-omp-harness.test.sh` full run from a clean tmux ancestor (fm-lab socket): 19 ok, 0 not ok, exit 0</code>\n- `Earlier: the nine watch-extension tests run with the ten earlier tests removed, all ok`\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Document** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⏭️ **Lint** - skipped</summary>\n\n- ⚠️ linter found issues (exit code 1)\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Push** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\nI am new to open source, and this pull request was made with AI assistance.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-13T05:23:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T03:37:59Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"258e7212a745e20ec67985dd0cdea29596443daf","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"i098:fix/fm-omp-watch-fixes","ref":"fix/fm-omp-watch-fixes","repo":{"id":1415958629,"node_id":"R_kgDOVGXQZQ","name":"firstmate-1","full_name":"i098/firstmate-1","owner":{"login":"i098","id":70973465,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTczNDY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70973465?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098","html_url":"https://github.com/i098","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i098/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Talk to one agent. Ship with a crew.","homepage":"","language":null,"visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"watchers":0,"open_issues_count":0,"open_issues":0,"size":48136,"default_branch":"main","has_issues":false,"has_projects":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_downloads":false,"has_discussions":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pushed_at":"2026-10-22T03:31:48Z","created_at":"2026-10-12T18:02:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T18:02:12Z","allow_forking":true,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","spdx_id":"MIT","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/i098/firstmate-1","html_url